651 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186240031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240651 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240651 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240651 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186240003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240651 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b832e88e-aa6a-556d-b56a-7bd0240d9f74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186238515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186238763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186238763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240683 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca08aa7d-69a4-53e7-9a42-33232fc442bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "847914f8-60db-55a2-9155-7cfe231e6bcb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241019 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$, $c=⟨-4,5,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,1,4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caedc8c2-ba3c-5e61-ad1f-0d5eafbb8652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241023 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ -2s+5t &=1 \\\\ -s-t &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "077cc4da-3c12-5749-87e3-9136fa56ff18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39d686df-f396-5c82-92b8-3b075c274d61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4dd5ec6b-997e-5c4c-82cd-f74e85dcbdf1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312909 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175